diff --git a/apps/reax/docs/decisions/0011-mobile-readers.md b/apps/reax/docs/decisions/0011-mobile-readers.md
new file mode 100644
index 0000000..bec35b4
--- /dev/null
+++ b/apps/reax/docs/decisions/0011-mobile-readers.md
@@ -0,0 +1,52 @@
+# 0011. Mobile readers: static APK and IPA inventories in memory
+
+Status: proposed (W2-6, MOB, first slice). To be recorded as D-42 to D-46 in
+`docs/implementation/DECISION-LOG.md` after review and green CI. ADR 0010 stays reserved for RUN.
+
+## Context
+
+The user's constraint: "MOB builds static APK and IPA readers only; ADB and Frida stay
+BLOCKED_EXTERNAL." No device, emulator, JDK, JADX, Apktool or SDK; nothing from the target is
+executed or extracted to disk. Core already lists zips (`parseZip`) but could not read an entry.
+
+## Decision
+
+- Two read-only operations, `inventory.apk` and `inventory.ipa`, over core's zip listing. Core gains
+  three non-result entry fields (`localHeaderOffset`, `crc32`, `flags`) and `zipEntryData` (D-43):
+  local header signature and name, method 0 or 8, no encryption, sizes within `maxBytes`, deflate
+  stopped one byte past the declared size, inflated length and CRC-32 checked; it never throws.
+- `src/readers/axml.ts` decodes Android binary XML; `src/readers/plist.ts` decodes XML and binary
+  plists; `src/readers/mobile.ts` holds `MOB_LIMITS` (frozen; 8 MiB and ratio 200 per entry read,
+  5000 entries, 1000 items per list, 65,536 characters per string; binary XML 65,536 strings,
+  100,000 elements, depth 64, 16 MiB of pool decoding; plist 100,000 objects, depth 64) and the
+  marker table. Tests lower limits only through `mobSeam`, never through a schema.
+- Ambiguity is never resolved by picking one (D-44): a target name listed twice, two `.app` bundles,
+  a local name that differs, overlapping local records give null values and partial.
+- An attribute is matched by its resource id where the resource map gives one; by name otherwise.
+- The key (D-45): `scripts/oracle-mob.py` (zipfile, plistlib, a struct binary-XML decoder) beside the
+  spec of `scripts/mob-fixtures.py` (struct and zlib only), both in `bench/oracle/mob.json`.
+
+- Shared references cannot amplify: every collecting loop (URL types, URL schemes, privacy
+  strings, permissions, components, markers) counts each item it examines, whatever its type, and
+  stops at the first item past `listItems` with a note; the passes over keys or elements that are
+  not collected are linear in the decoded objects or elements. An over-long URL scheme or privacy
+  key is left out (never `""`), with one note however often it is reached. A binary plist counts
+  every reference it follows against `plist.refs` (200,000), and the bytes its objects claim may not
+  exceed the object area, so objects that share bytes are refused before they are decoded. Each
+  decoder keeps at most 100 notes (`axml.notes`, `plist.notes`) and one count of the rest; reported
+  notes are deduplicated and capped at 50, then one count. The manifest's element pass is linear.
+- **Third-party cross-check (once, offline, by hand; D-10's precedent).** pyaxmlparser 0.3.31
+  (Apache-2.0; wheel sha256 3c6609a4…494f), with lxml 5.3.0 (prebuilt wheel, sha256 1ffc2301…c5de),
+  click 8.1.7 and asn1crypto 1.5.1 (licences: lxml BSD-3-Clause, click BSD-3-Clause, asn1crypto
+  MIT; none pulls in frida or a native build), downloaded from PyPI and installed hash-locked with `--no-deps --no-index` in
+  `/tmp/mob-axml-venv`, run as a separate process by `scripts/oracle-mob-crosscheck.py`. On every
+  positive APK fixture the package, versions, SDKs, permissions and components equal the key, except
+  `mob-idswap.apk`: pyaxmlparser matches an attribute by its name string, reax and the key by its
+  resource id (this ADR's rule). On the damaged fixtures pyaxmlparser is lenient (U+FFFD, `""` for
+  an index out of range, reading past chunk sizes) where reax gives null and partial.
+
+## Out of scope
+
+.NET metadata (a later MOB slice), DEX, `resources.arsc` (references are reported as `@0x…`), APK
+signatures, `embedded.mobileprovision`, entitlements, nested `.appex` and Watch bundles, Flutter
+snapshot hashes, a standalone plist operation (ARC).
