diff --git a/apps/reax/docs/operations.md b/apps/reax/docs/operations.md
index 369cb2a..fba84b2 100644
--- a/apps/reax/docs/operations.md
+++ b/apps/reax/docs/operations.md
@@ -364,6 +364,58 @@ Result includes:
 
 Ledger rows: `rea.tool/inspect_rust_binary`, `leanrea/LEAN-C29`, `leanrea/LEAN-T13`.
 
+### `inventory.apk`
+
+An Android APK read in memory, nothing extracted: the zip listing (paged), the binary AndroidManifest.xml's package, version code and name, min and target SDK, requested permissions and components (activity, activity-alias, service, receiver, provider; name, exported), and framework markers from exact listing paths (Flutter, React Native Hermes). Bounded (8 MiB and a ratio of 200 per entry read, 5000 entries); damage or ambiguity (a name listed twice, overlapping entries) gives null values and partial.
+
+Effect: read. Cost: cheap. Output from the target is untrusted (sent inside the untrusted-content envelope). Platforms: linux, darwin, win32.
+
+| Argument | Type | Required | Default | Meaning |
+|---|---|---|---|---|
+| `path` | string (≤ 4096 chars) | yes |  | File path inside the workspace |
+| `offset` | integer (≥ 0) | no | `0` | first row to return (page.next continues) |
+| `limit` | integer (≥ 1, ≤ 10000) | no | `200` | rows per page |
+
+Example: What an APK asks for and declares.
+
+```json
+{"operation":"inventory.apk","path":"mob-app.apk"}
+```
+
+Result includes:
+
+```json
+{"manifest":{"package":"com.reax.fixture","versionCode":42,"minSdkVersion":21},"markers":[{"framework":"Flutter","evidence":"lib/arm64-v8a/libflutter.so","next":"blutter"}]}
+```
+
+Ledger rows: `leanrea/LEAN-T08`.
+
+### `inventory.ipa`
+
+An iOS IPA read in memory, nothing extracted: the zip listing (paged), the one Payload/<name>.app/Info.plist (XML or binary): bundle id, executable, versions, minimum OS, URL schemes and privacy usage strings; and framework markers (Flutter.framework, hermes.framework). Bounded (8 MiB and a ratio of 200 per entry read, 5000 entries); two app bundles, a duplicated or damaged plist give null values and partial.
+
+Effect: read. Cost: cheap. Output from the target is untrusted (sent inside the untrusted-content envelope). Platforms: linux, darwin, win32.
+
+| Argument | Type | Required | Default | Meaning |
+|---|---|---|---|---|
+| `path` | string (≤ 4096 chars) | yes |  | File path inside the workspace |
+| `offset` | integer (≥ 0) | no | `0` | first row to return (page.next continues) |
+| `limit` | integer (≥ 1, ≤ 10000) | no | `200` | rows per page |
+
+Example: What an iOS app is and which privacy strings it shows.
+
+```json
+{"operation":"inventory.ipa","path":"mob-xml.ipa"}
+```
+
+Result includes:
+
+```json
+{"app":"Payload/Reax.app/","info":{"CFBundleIdentifier":"com.reax.fixture","urlSchemes":["reax","reax-dev","fb123456"]}}
+```
+
+Ledger rows: `leanrea/LEAN-T17`.
+
 ## read
 
 ### `read.strings`
